# Angular Frontend: Patient Management System

A minimal, production-style Angular 17 frontend that integrates with the existing Spring Cloud Gateway and demonstrates TypeScript skills, reactive forms, REST integration, auth flow, and testing.

## A) Backend Endpoints Found

All patient routes require a `Bearer <token>` header (enforced by gateway JWT filter).

| Method | URL (via Gateway @ port 4004) | Description |
|--------|-------------------------------|-------------|
| `POST` | `http://localhost:4004/auth/login` | Login → returns `{ token: string }` |
| `GET`  | `http://localhost:4004/api/patients` | List all patients → `PatientResponse[]` |
| `POST` | `http://localhost:4004/api/patients` | Create patient → [PatientResponse](file:///d:/workspace/patient_management_system/patient-service/src/main/java/com/pm/patientservice/dto/PatientResponseDTO.java#3-50) (201) |
| `PUT`  | `http://localhost:4004/api/patients/{id}` | Update patient → [PatientResponse](file:///d:/workspace/patient_management_system/patient-service/src/main/java/com/pm/patientservice/dto/PatientResponseDTO.java#3-50) (200) |
| `DELETE` | `http://localhost:4004/api/patients/{id}` | Delete patient → `204 No Content` |

> **Note**: No GET-by-id endpoint exists in the backend. Patient detail view will use the list data (fetch all, find by id client-side), with a clear TODO comment.

> **Note**: No server-side search/pagination. Client-side search + pagination will be implemented with a clear TODO comment.

### Error Response Shape
```json
{
  "timestamp": "...", "status": 400, "error": "Bad Request",
  "message": "Validation failed...", "path": "/patients",
  "details": { "fieldErrors": { "email": "Email should be valid" } }
}
```

