## Proposed Changes

### [NEW] Frontend Project — `d:\workspace\patient_management_system\frontend\`

#### [NEW] package.json / angular.json / tsconfig.json
Standard Angular 17 CLI scaffold via `ng new`. Scripts: `start`, `test`, `build`.

---

#### [NEW] environments/environment.ts
```ts
export const environment = { apiBaseUrl: 'http://localhost:4004' };
```

---

#### [NEW] core/models/patient.model.ts
TypeScript interfaces matching backend DTOs:
- [PatientRequest](file:///d:/workspace/patient_management_system/patient-service/src/main/java/com/pm/patientservice/dto/PatientRequestDTO.java#10-73) — name, email, address, dateOfBirth, registeredDate
- [PatientResponse](file:///d:/workspace/patient_management_system/patient-service/src/main/java/com/pm/patientservice/dto/PatientResponseDTO.java#3-50) — id, name, email, address, dateOfBirth
- `BackendError` — timestamp, status, error, message, path, details

---

#### [NEW] core/models/auth.model.ts
- [LoginRequest](file:///d:/workspace/patient_management_system/auth-service/src/main/java/com/pm/authservice/dto/LoginRequestDTO.java#7-32) — email, password
- `LoginResponse` — token

---

#### [NEW] core/services/auth-state.service.ts
- Stores JWT token in a private field and `localStorage`
- `setToken(token)`, `getToken()`, `clearToken()`, `isLoggedIn()`

---

#### [NEW] core/services/auth-api.service.ts
- [login(req: LoginRequest): Observable<LoginResponse>](file:///d:/workspace/patient_management_system/auth-service/src/main/java/com/pm/authservice/controller/AuthController.java#26-40) → `POST /auth/login`

---

#### [NEW] core/services/patient-api.service.ts
- [getAll(): Observable<PatientResponse[]>](file:///d:/workspace/patient_management_system/patient-service/src/main/java/com/pm/patientservice/controller/PatientController.java#31-37) → `GET /api/patients`
- [create(p: PatientRequest): Observable<PatientResponse>](file:///d:/workspace/patient_management_system/patient-service/src/main/java/com/pm/patientservice/controller/PatientController.java#45-53) → `POST /api/patients`
- [update(id: string, p: PatientRequest): Observable<PatientResponse>](file:///d:/workspace/patient_management_system/patient-service/src/main/java/com/pm/patientservice/controller/PatientController.java#54-63) → `PUT /api/patients/{id}`
- [delete(id: string): Observable<void>](file:///d:/workspace/patient_management_system/patient-service/src/main/java/com/pm/patientservice/controller/PatientController.java#64-71) → `DELETE /api/patients/{id}`

---

#### [NEW] core/interceptors/auth.interceptor.ts
Functional interceptor (`HttpInterceptorFn`):
- Reads token from `AuthStateService`; attaches `Authorization: Bearer <token>` if present
- Catches `401` response → calls `AuthStateService.clearToken()` → `router.navigate(['/login'])`

---

#### [NEW] core/guards/auth.guard.ts
Functional `CanActivateFn`:
- Returns `true` if token exists, else navigates to `/login`

---

#### [NEW] features/login/login.component.ts
- Standalone component with Angular Material `mat-form-field`, reactive form
- Fields: email (required + email validator), password (required + minLength 8)
- On submit: calls `AuthApiService.login()`, stores token, redirects to `/patients`
- Displays API error message on 401

---

#### [NEW] features/patient-list/patient-list.component.ts
- Loads all patients on init via `PatientApiService.getAll()`
- Client-side search with `debounceTime(300)` on search input (RxJS + TODO server-side search)
- Client-side pagination (page size: 10, TODO: server-side)
- `mat-table` with columns: name, email, dateOfBirth, address + actions
- Row click → `/patients/:id`
- Loading spinner + error banner states

---

#### [NEW] features/patient-create/patient-create.component.ts
- Reactive form: name (required, max 100), email (required, email format), address (required, max 255), dateOfBirth (required, YYYY-MM-DD pattern), registeredDate (required, YYYY-MM-DD pattern)
- Shows inline field errors from both Angular validators and backend `fieldErrors`
- On submit: calls `PatientApiService.create()`, navigates to `/patients/:id`

---

#### [NEW] features/patient-detail/patient-detail.component.ts
- Loads patient from list (client-side lookup by id), shows detail view
- Toggle edit mode → same reactive form as create (minus registeredDate)
- Delete button → opens `ConfirmDialogComponent` → calls `PatientApiService.delete()` → navigates to `/patients`

---

#### [NEW] shared/confirm-dialog/confirm-dialog.component.ts
- Simple Angular Material `mat-dialog` with "Confirm" and "Cancel" buttons

---

#### [NEW] frontend/README.md
- Prerequisites, run instructions, API base URL config, demo flow

---

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests (run locally)

First, install dependencies:
```bash
cd d:\workspace\patient_management_system\frontend
npm install
```

Run all tests (headless):
```bash
npm test -- --watch=false --browsers=ChromeHeadless
```

**Test 1** — `patient-api.service.spec.ts`: Uses `HttpTestingController` to verify [getAll()](file:///d:/workspace/patient_management_system/patient-service/src/main/java/com/pm/patientservice/controller/PatientController.java#31-37) makes `GET /api/patients`, [create()](file:///d:/workspace/patient_management_system/patient-service/src/main/java/com/pm/patientservice/controller/PatientController.java#45-53) makes `POST /api/patients`, [delete()](file:///d:/workspace/patient_management_system/patient-service/src/main/java/com/pm/patientservice/controller/PatientController.java#64-71) makes `DELETE /api/patients/{id}`.

**Test 2** — `patient-create.component.spec.ts`: Renders form, submits empty → checks required errors appear on all fields. Submits invalid email → checks email error.

**Test 3** — `patient-list.component.spec.ts`: Provides mock `PatientApiService` returning 2 patients. Checks table rows are rendered. Checks search input filters the list.

### Manual Smoke Test (requires running backend)
1. Start backend: `docker-compose up -d` (or run patient-service on :4000, auth-service on :4005, gateway on :4004)
2. Start frontend: `npm start` (opens at `http://localhost:4200`)
3. Navigate to `http://localhost:4200` → should redirect to `/login`
4. Log in with valid credentials → should redirect to `/patients`
5. Create a patient via `/patients/new` → should appear in the list
6. Click a patient row → should show detail view
7. Edit the patient → save → verify changes
8. Delete the patient → confirm → should be removed from list
